---Contains all of the attributes of a specific cluster.
---@class aws.elasticache.CacheCluster
---@field CacheClusterId? aws.elasticache.String The user-supplied identifier of the cluster. This identifier is a unique key that identifies a cluster.
---@field ConfigurationEndpoint? aws.elasticache.Endpoint Represents a Memcached cluster endpoint which can be used by an application to connect to any node in the cluster. The configuration endpoint will always have .cfg in it.
---@field ClientDownloadLandingPage? aws.elasticache.String The URL of the web page where you can download the latest ElastiCache client library.
---@field CacheNodeType? aws.elasticache.String The name of the compute and memory capacity node type for the cluster.
---@field Engine? aws.elasticache.String The name of the cache engine (memcached or redis) to be used for this cluster.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.elasticache.String The version of the cache engine that is used in this cluster.
---@field CacheClusterStatus? aws.elasticache.String The current state of this cluster, one of the following values: available, creating, deleted, deleting, incompatible-network, modifying, rebooting cluster nodes, restore-failed, or snapshotting.
---@field NumCacheNodes? aws.elasticache.IntegerOptional The number of cache nodes in the cluster.
---@field PreferredAvailabilityZone? aws.elasticache.String The name of the Availability Zone in which the cluster is located or "Multiple" if the cache nodes are located in different Availability Zones.
---@field PreferredOutpostArn? aws.elasticache.String The outpost ARN in which the cache cluster is created.
---@field CacheClusterCreateTime? aws.elasticache.TStamp The date and time when the cluster was created.
---@field PreferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.elasticache.String Specifies the weekly time range during which maintenance on the cluster is performed. It is specified as a range in the format ddd:hh24:mi-ddd:hh24:mi (24H Clock UTC). The minimum maintenance window is a 60 minute period.
---@field PendingModifiedValues? aws.elasticache.PendingModifiedValues
---@field NotificationConfiguration? aws.elasticache.NotificationConfiguration Describes a notification topic and its status. Notification topics are used for publishing ElastiCache events to subscribers using Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS).
---@field CacheSecurityGroups? aws.elasticache.CacheSecurityGroupMembershipList A list of cache security group elements, composed of name and status sub-elements.
---@field CacheParameterGroup? aws.elasticache.CacheParameterGroupStatus Status of the cache parameter group.
---@field CacheSubnetGroupName? aws.elasticache.String The name of the cache subnet group associated with the cluster.
---@field CacheNodes? aws.elasticache.CacheNodeList A list of cache nodes that are members of the cluster.
---@field AutoMinorVersionUpgrade? aws.elasticache.Boolean If you are running Valkey or Redis OSS engine version 6.0 or later, set this parameter to yes if you want to opt-in to the next auto minor version upgrade campaign. This parameter is disabled for previous versions.
---@field SecurityGroups? aws.elasticache.SecurityGroupMembershipList A list of VPC Security Groups associated with the cluster.
---@field ReplicationGroupId? aws.elasticache.String The replication group to which this cluster belongs. If this field is empty, the cluster is not associated with any replication group.
---@field SnapshotRetentionLimit? aws.elasticache.IntegerOptional The number of days for which ElastiCache retains automatic cluster snapshots before deleting them. For example, if you set SnapshotRetentionLimit to 5, a snapshot that was taken today is retained for 5 days before being deleted.
---@field SnapshotWindow? aws.elasticache.String The daily time range (in UTC) during which ElastiCache begins taking a daily snapshot of your cluster.
---@field AuthTokenEnabled? aws.elasticache.BooleanOptional A flag that enables using an AuthToken (password) when issuing Valkey or Redis OSS commands.
---@field AuthTokenLastModifiedDate? aws.elasticache.TStamp The date the auth token was last modified
---@field TransitEncryptionEnabled? aws.elasticache.BooleanOptional A flag that enables in-transit encryption when set to true.
---@field AtRestEncryptionEnabled? aws.elasticache.BooleanOptional A flag that enables encryption at-rest when set to true.
---@field ARN? aws.elasticache.String The ARN (Amazon Resource Name) of the cache cluster.
---@field ReplicationGroupLogDeliveryEnabled? aws.elasticache.Boolean A boolean value indicating whether log delivery is enabled for the replication group.
---@field LogDeliveryConfigurations? aws.elasticache.LogDeliveryConfigurationList Returns the destination, format and type of the logs.
---@field NetworkType? aws.elasticache.NetworkType Must be either ipv4 | ipv6 | dual_stack. IPv6 is supported for workloads using Valkey 7.2 and above, Redis OSS engine version 6.2 7.1 or Memcached engine version 1.6.6 and above on all instances built on the Nitro system.
---@field IpDiscovery? aws.elasticache.IpDiscovery The network type associated with the cluster, either ipv4 | ipv6. IPv6 is supported for workloads using Valkey 7.2 and above, Redis OSS engine version 6.2 to 7.1 or Memcached engine version 1.6.6 and above on all instances built on the Nitro system.
---@field TransitEncryptionMode? aws.elasticache.TransitEncryptionMode A setting that allows you to migrate your clients to use in-transit encryption, with no downtime.

