---Represents the input of a CreateCacheCluster operation.
---@class aws.elasticache.CreateCacheClusterMessage
---@field CacheClusterId aws.elasticache.String The node group (shard) identifier. This parameter is stored as a lowercase string.
---@field ReplicationGroupId? aws.elasticache.String The ID of the replication group to which this cluster should belong. If this parameter is specified, the cluster is added to the specified replication group as a read replica; otherwise, the cluster is a standalone primary that is not part of any replication group.
---@field AZMode? aws.elasticache.AZMode|string Specifies whether the nodes in this Memcached cluster are created in a single Availability Zone or created across multiple Availability Zones in the cluster's region.
---@field PreferredAvailabilityZone? aws.elasticache.String The EC2 Availability Zone in which the cluster is created.
---@field PreferredAvailabilityZones? aws.elasticache.PreferredAvailabilityZoneList A list of the Availability Zones in which cache nodes are created. The order of the zones in the list is not important.
---@field NumCacheNodes? aws.elasticache.IntegerOptional The initial number of cache nodes that the cluster has.
---@field CacheNodeType? aws.elasticache.String The compute and memory capacity of the nodes in the node group (shard).
---@field Engine? aws.elasticache.String The name of the cache engine to be used for this cluster.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.elasticache.String The version number of the cache engine to be used for this cluster. To view the supported cache engine versions, use the DescribeCacheEngineVersions operation.
---@field CacheParameterGroupName? aws.elasticache.String The name of the parameter group to associate with this cluster. If this argument is omitted, the default parameter group for the specified engine is used. You cannot use any parameter group which has cluster-enabled='yes' when creating a cluster.
---@field CacheSubnetGroupName? aws.elasticache.String The name of the subnet group to be used for the cluster.
---@field CacheSecurityGroupNames? aws.elasticache.CacheSecurityGroupNameList A list of security group names to associate with this cluster.
---@field SecurityGroupIds? aws.elasticache.SecurityGroupIdsList One or more VPC security groups associated with the cluster.
---@field Tags? aws.elasticache.TagList A list of tags to be added to this resource.
---@field SnapshotArns? aws.elasticache.SnapshotArnsList A single-element string list containing an Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that uniquely identifies a Valkey or Redis OSS RDB snapshot file stored in Amazon S3. The snapshot file is used to populate the node group (shard). The Amazon S3 object name in the ARN cannot contain any commas.
---@field SnapshotName? aws.elasticache.String The name of a Valkey or Redis OSS snapshot from which to restore data into the new node group (shard). The snapshot status changes to restoring while the new node group (shard) is being created.
---@field PreferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.elasticache.String Specifies the weekly time range during which maintenance on the cluster is performed. It is specified as a range in the format ddd:hh24:mi-ddd:hh24:mi (24H Clock UTC). The minimum maintenance window is a 60 minute period.
