---Contains all of the attributes of a specific Valkey or Redis OSS replication group.
---@class aws.elasticache.ReplicationGroup
---@field ReplicationGroupId? aws.elasticache.String The identifier for the replication group.
---@field Description? aws.elasticache.String The user supplied description of the replication group.
---@field GlobalReplicationGroupInfo? aws.elasticache.GlobalReplicationGroupInfo The name of the Global datastore and role of this replication group in the Global datastore.
---@field Status? aws.elasticache.String The current state of this replication group - creating, available, modifying, deleting, create-failed, snapshotting.
---@field PendingModifiedValues? aws.elasticache.ReplicationGroupPendingModifiedValues A group of settings to be applied to the replication group, either immediately or during the next maintenance window.
---@field MemberClusters? aws.elasticache.ClusterIdList The names of all the cache clusters that are part of this replication group.
---@field NodeGroups? aws.elasticache.NodeGroupList A list of node groups in this replication group. For Valkey or Redis OSS (cluster mode disabled) replication groups, this is a single-element list. For Valkey or Redis OSS (cluster mode enabled) replication groups, the list contains an entry for each node group (shard).
---@field SnapshottingClusterId? aws.elasticache.String The cluster ID that is used as the daily snapshot source for the replication group.
---@field AutomaticFailover? aws.elasticache.AutomaticFailoverStatus Indicates the status of automatic failover for this Valkey or Redis OSS replication group.
---@field MultiAZ? aws.elasticache.MultiAZStatus A flag indicating if you have Multi-AZ enabled to enhance fault tolerance. For more information, see Minimizing Downtime: Multi-AZ
---@field ConfigurationEndpoint? aws.elasticache.Endpoint The configuration endpoint for this replication group. Use the configuration endpoint to connect to this replication group.
---@field SnapshotRetentionLimit? aws.elasticache.IntegerOptional The number of days for which ElastiCache retains automatic cluster snapshots before deleting them. For example, if you set SnapshotRetentionLimit to 5, a snapshot that was taken today is retained for 5 days before being deleted.
---@field SnapshotWindow? aws.elasticache.String The daily time range (in UTC) during which ElastiCache begins taking a daily snapshot of your node group (shard).
---@field ClusterEnabled? aws.elasticache.BooleanOptional A flag indicating whether or not this replication group is cluster enabled; i.e., whether its data can be partitioned across multiple shards (API/CLI: node groups).
---@field CacheNodeType? aws.elasticache.String The name of the compute and memory capacity node type for each node in the replication group.
---@field AuthTokenEnabled? aws.elasticache.BooleanOptional A flag that enables using an AuthToken (password) when issuing Valkey or Redis OSS commands.
---@field AuthTokenLastModifiedDate? aws.elasticache.TStamp The date the auth token was last modified
---@field TransitEncryptionEnabled? aws.elasticache.BooleanOptional A flag that enables in-transit encryption when set to true.
---@field AtRestEncryptionEnabled? aws.elasticache.BooleanOptional A flag that enables encryption at-rest on the cluster when set to true. In some cases, encryption at-rest may be enabled even when this value is false. Use StorageEncryptionType to view the effective encryption state of a cluster.
---@field MemberClustersOutpostArns? aws.elasticache.ReplicationGroupOutpostArnList The outpost ARNs of the replication group's member clusters.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.elasticache.String The ID of the KMS key used to encrypt the disk in the cluster.
---@field StorageEncryptionType? aws.elasticache.StorageEncryptionType Indicates the type of encryption for data stored at rest in the replication group. The value is none if at-rest encryption is not enabled, sse-elasticache if an ElastiCache service-managed key is used, or sse-kms if a customer-managed KMS key is used.
---@field ARN? aws.elasticache.String The ARN (Amazon Resource Name) of the replication group.
---@field UserGroupIds? aws.elasticache.UserGroupIdList The ID of the user group associated to the replication group.
---@field LogDeliveryConfigurations? aws.elasticache.LogDeliveryConfigurationList Returns the destination, format and type of the logs.
---@field ReplicationGroupCreateTime? aws.elasticache.TStamp The date and time when the cluster was created.
---@field DataTiering? aws.elasticache.DataTieringStatus Enables data tiering. Data tiering is only supported for replication groups using the r6gd node type. This parameter must be set to true when using r6gd nodes. For more information, see Data tiering.
---@field AutoMinorVersionUpgrade? aws.elasticache.Boolean If you are running Valkey 7.2 and above, or Redis OSS engine version 6.0 and above, set this parameter to yes if you want to opt-in to the next auto minor version upgrade campaign. This parameter is disabled for previous versions.
---@field NetworkType? aws.elasticache.NetworkType Must be either ipv4 | ipv6 | dual_stack. IPv6 is supported for workloads using Valkey 7.2 and above, Redis OSS engine version 6.2 to 7.1 or Memcached engine version 1.6.6 and above on all instances built on the Nitro system.
---@field IpDiscovery? aws.elasticache.IpDiscovery The network type you choose when modifying a cluster, either ipv4 | ipv6. IPv6 is supported for workloads using Valkey 7.2 and above, Redis OSS engine version 6.2 to 7.1 or Memcached engine version 1.6.6 and above on all instances built on the Nitro system.
---@field TransitEncryptionMode? aws.elasticache.TransitEncryptionMode A setting that allows you to migrate your clients to use in-transit encryption, with no downtime.
---@field ClusterMode? aws.elasticache.ClusterMode Enabled or Disabled. To modify cluster mode from Disabled to Enabled, you must first set the cluster mode to Compatible. Compatible mode allows your Valkey or Redis OSS clients to connect using both cluster mode enabled and cluster mode disabled. After you migrate all Valkey or Redis OSS clients to use cluster mode enabled, you can then complete cluster mode configuration and set the cluster mode ...
---@field Engine? aws.elasticache.String The engine used in a replication group. The options are valkey, memcached or redis.
---@field Durability? aws.elasticache.Durability The durability setting of the replication group. For more information, see Durability.
---@field EffectiveDurability? aws.elasticache.EffectiveDurability The effective durability of the replication group. When Durability is set to default, the service resolves the actual durability based on the engine version, cluster mode, and other parameters. This field reflects the resolved value. For more information, see Configuring Durability.

---@alias aws.elasticache.ReplicationGroupIdList aws.elasticache.String[]

---@alias aws.elasticache.ReplicationGroupList aws.elasticache.ReplicationGroup[]

