---The resource representing a serverless cache.
---@class aws.elasticache.ServerlessCache
---@field ServerlessCacheName? aws.elasticache.String The unique identifier of the serverless cache.
---@field Description? aws.elasticache.String A description of the serverless cache.
---@field CreateTime? aws.elasticache.TStamp When the serverless cache was created.
---@field Status? aws.elasticache.String The current status of the serverless cache. The allowed values are CREATING, AVAILABLE, DELETING, CREATE-FAILED and MODIFYING.
---@field Engine? aws.elasticache.String The engine the serverless cache is compatible with.
---@field MajorEngineVersion? aws.elasticache.String The version number of the engine the serverless cache is compatible with.
---@field FullEngineVersion? aws.elasticache.String The name and version number of the engine the serverless cache is compatible with.
---@field CacheUsageLimits? aws.elasticache.CacheUsageLimits The cache usage limit for the serverless cache.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.elasticache.String The ID of the Amazon Web Services Key Management Service (KMS) key that is used to encrypt data at rest in the serverless cache.
---@field StorageEncryptionType? aws.elasticache.StorageEncryptionType Indicates the type of encryption for data stored at rest in the serverless cache. Serverless caches are always encrypted at rest. The value is sse-elasticache if an ElastiCache service-managed key is used, or sse-kms if a customer-managed KMS key is used.
---@field SecurityGroupIds? aws.elasticache.SecurityGroupIdsList The IDs of the EC2 security groups associated with the serverless cache.
---@field Endpoint? aws.elasticache.Endpoint
---@field ReaderEndpoint? aws.elasticache.Endpoint
---@field ARN? aws.elasticache.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the serverless cache.
---@field UserGroupId? aws.elasticache.String The identifier of the user group associated with the serverless cache. Available for Valkey and Redis OSS only. Default is NULL.
---@field SubnetIds? aws.elasticache.SubnetIdsList If no subnet IDs are given and your VPC is in us-west-1, then ElastiCache will select 2 default subnets across AZs in your VPC. For all other Regions, if no subnet IDs are given then ElastiCache will select 3 default subnets across AZs in your default VPC.
---@field SnapshotRetentionLimit? aws.elasticache.IntegerOptional The number of days for which ElastiCache retains automatic snapshots before deleting them. Available for Valkey, Redis OSS and Serverless Memcached only. The maximum value allowed is 35 days.
---@field DailySnapshotTime? aws.elasticache.String The daily time that a cache snapshot will be created. Default is NULL, i.e. snapshots will not be created at a specific time on a daily basis. Available for Valkey, Redis OSS and Serverless Memcached only.
---@field NetworkType? aws.elasticache.NetworkType The type of IP address protocol used by the serverless cache. Must be either ipv4 | ipv6 | dual_stack. ipv6 is only supported with IPv6-only subnets. If not specified, defaults to ipv4, unless all provided subnets are IPv6-only, in which case it defaults to ipv6.
---@field ConnectionType? aws.elasticache.ConnectionType The connection type for the serverless cache. Must be either vpc | public. If not specified, defaults to vpc.
---@field Migration? aws.elasticache.MigrationSummary Provides a summary of the migration status for the serverless cache.

