---Represents a copy of an entire Valkey or Redis OSS cluster as of the time when the snapshot was taken.
---@class aws.elasticache.Snapshot
---@field SnapshotName? aws.elasticache.String The name of a snapshot. For an automatic snapshot, the name is system-generated. For a manual snapshot, this is the user-provided name.
---@field ReplicationGroupId? aws.elasticache.String The unique identifier of the source replication group.
---@field ReplicationGroupDescription? aws.elasticache.String A description of the source replication group.
---@field CacheClusterId? aws.elasticache.String The user-supplied identifier of the source cluster.
---@field SnapshotStatus? aws.elasticache.String The status of the snapshot. Valid values: creating | available | restoring | copying | deleting.
---@field SnapshotSource? aws.elasticache.String Indicates whether the snapshot is from an automatic backup (automated) or was created manually (manual).
---@field CacheNodeType? aws.elasticache.String The name of the compute and memory capacity node type for the source cluster.
---@field Engine? aws.elasticache.String The name of the cache engine (memcached or redis) used by the source cluster.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.elasticache.String The version of the cache engine version that is used by the source cluster.
---@field NumCacheNodes? aws.elasticache.IntegerOptional The number of cache nodes in the source cluster.
---@field PreferredAvailabilityZone? aws.elasticache.String The name of the Availability Zone in which the source cluster is located.
---@field PreferredOutpostArn? aws.elasticache.String The ARN (Amazon Resource Name) of the preferred outpost.
---@field CacheClusterCreateTime? aws.elasticache.TStamp The date and time when the source cluster was created.
---@field PreferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.elasticache.String Specifies the weekly time range during which maintenance on the cluster is performed. It is specified as a range in the format ddd:hh24:mi-ddd:hh24:mi (24H Clock UTC). The minimum maintenance window is a 60 minute period.
---@field TopicArn? aws.elasticache.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the topic used by the source cluster for publishing notifications.
---@field Port? aws.elasticache.IntegerOptional The port number used by each cache nodes in the source cluster.
---@field CacheParameterGroupName? aws.elasticache.String The cache parameter group that is associated with the source cluster.
---@field CacheSubnetGroupName? aws.elasticache.String The name of the cache subnet group associated with the source cluster.
---@field VpcId? aws.elasticache.String The Amazon Virtual Private Cloud identifier (VPC ID) of the cache subnet group for the source cluster.
---@field AutoMinorVersionUpgrade? aws.elasticache.Boolean If you are running Valkey 7.2 and above or Redis OSS engine version 6.0 and above, set this parameter to yes if you want to opt-in to the next auto minor version upgrade campaign. This parameter is disabled for previous versions.
---@field SnapshotRetentionLimit? aws.elasticache.IntegerOptional For an automatic snapshot, the number of days for which ElastiCache retains the snapshot before deleting it.
---@field SnapshotWindow? aws.elasticache.String The daily time range during which ElastiCache takes daily snapshots of the source cluster.
---@field NumNodeGroups? aws.elasticache.IntegerOptional The number of node groups (shards) in this snapshot. When restoring from a snapshot, the number of node groups (shards) in the snapshot and in the restored replication group must be the same.
---@field AutomaticFailover? aws.elasticache.AutomaticFailoverStatus Indicates the status of automatic failover for the source Valkey or Redis OSS replication group.
---@field NodeSnapshots? aws.elasticache.NodeSnapshotList A list of the cache nodes in the source cluster.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.elasticache.String The ID of the KMS key used to encrypt the snapshot.
---@field ARN? aws.elasticache.String The ARN (Amazon Resource Name) of the snapshot.
---@field DataTiering? aws.elasticache.DataTieringStatus Enables data tiering. Data tiering is only supported for replication groups using the r6gd node type. This parameter must be set to true when using r6gd nodes. For more information, see Data tiering.
---@field Durability? aws.elasticache.Durability The durability setting of the cluster when the snapshot was taken. When restoring from this snapshot, the cluster uses this durability setting unless overridden in the restore request. For more information, see Durability.

